WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:06.210
Film Courage: Is there a specific kind of
story a first-time screenwriter should make?

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:11.460
Larry Wilson: Ah…Yes!

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:17.009
What that story is and it’s not that cliche
of ‘Write what you know’ because I’ve

00:00:17.009 --> 00:00:20.220
never written what I “know.”

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:28.850
I write fantastical worlds and supernatural
stories and all of that.

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:33.080
But write what you feel and what’s in your
heart and write something that means something

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:34.500
to you.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.350
And you know I was a script reader for gosh…probably
a decade.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:48.080
And I was reading 7-8 scripts a week.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:51.510
And the rare one was the great script.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:56.380
And when I found that, this was a very exciting
day at the office.

00:00:56.380 --> 00:01:03.280
And sometimes the really terrible scripts,
they were fun because they were so God-awful.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:08.229
But the ones that got really exhausting and
really irritating as a script reader who has

00:01:08.229 --> 00:01:14.021
to read a script, synopsize it, write a comment
about it, and then pick up another one, read

00:01:14.021 --> 00:01:19.409
it and synopsize it, were ones who you could
tell were written by people who were looking

00:01:19.409 --> 00:01:24.880
at what last year’s hit was and trying to
imitate it.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:28.670
And those were deadly!

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:30.640
And they weren’t good.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.450
They weren’t bad.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:36.289
They were safe and mediocre.

00:01:36.289 --> 00:01:45.259
And any young writer or old writer, anyone
who is just starting to write, write something

00:01:45.259 --> 00:01:47.700
that you feel.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:50.060
Write something that comes from the heart.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:54.569
And people may not think that BEETLEJUICE
is a personal movie but it’s an intensely

00:01:54.569 --> 00:01:55.569
personal movie.

00:01:55.569 --> 00:01:59.969
It was intensely personal for Michael [the
co-writer].

00:01:59.969 --> 00:02:07.229
And I didn’t know that I had a theme until
I had enough work to realize I had a theme.

00:02:07.229 --> 00:02:13.540
And almost everything I’ve written are about
broken families who are put back together

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:25.250
in some bizarre way because I came from a
broken family.

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:31.760
So I like to think that my work has a sense
of heart and a sense of compassion and a sense

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:33.400
of humanity.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:39.349
No matter how bizarre it is, no matter how
weird the worlds get.

00:02:39.349 --> 00:02:45.130
And you’ve got to write something that you
feel, that you have some passion for or why

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:46.130
do it?

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:48.579
It’s just too hard.

00:02:48.579 --> 00:02:51.500
It’s not an easy job.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:58.550
I personally can’t imagine saying “Well,
this was a hit.

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:03.310
So now I am going to write my version of that.

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:07.620
It’s not really what I care about, what
I feel.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:08.980
But I can imitate it well enough.”

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:12.650
I can’t imagine spending a year of your
life doing that.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:14.569
But people do it all the time.

00:03:14.569 --> 00:03:17.970
And people usually write mediocre scripts.

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:22.360
Film Courage: Is being safe something that
has never appealed to you?

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:28.799
Larry Wilson: I don’t know how…in my career
and in my life!

00:03:28.799 --> 00:03:35.489
Safe hasn’t factored into it.

00:03:35.489 --> 00:03:39.049
Not always the best decision, maybe?

00:03:39.049 --> 00:03:42.709
But I sort of like jumping off cliffs.

